    <article class="container">
        <h1>Mat Pilates in Lagos</h1>
        <p style="color:#aaa; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:40px;">Classical mat work on Praia da Batata. No reformers. No machines. Just your body and the mat.</p>
        
        <h2>Why Mat Pilates?</h2>
        <p>Joseph Pilates created his method on the mat first. The reformer and cadillac came later as modifications. At Heat Lagos, we return to the source — classical mat Pilates that builds core strength, spinal alignment, and full-body control using nothing but your body weight and precise movement.</p>
        
        <p>This is Pilates as it was intended:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Bodyweight resistance:</strong> No springs, no pulleys, no external load</li>
            <li><strong>Precision over speed:</strong> Every movement is controlled and intentional</li>
            <li><strong>Core-centric:</strong> Every exercise starts from the center and radiates outward</li>
            <li><strong>Full-body integration:</strong> Arms, legs, spine, and breath work together</li>
            <li><strong>Progressive difficulty:</strong> Beginner to advanced variations of every exercise</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="highlight-box">
            <h3>Mat Pilates vs Reformer Pilates</h3>
            <p>Reformer Pilates uses a machine with springs and pulleys to provide resistance. It's great for rehabilitation and controlled movement. But mat Pilates is where the real work happens — you support your own weight, you create your own resistance, and you develop the kind of core strength that transfers to every other physical activity.</p>
            <p>At Heat Lagos, we don't have reformers because we believe in the purity of the mat method. Your body is the machine.</p>
        </div>
        
        <h2>The Class Experience</h2>
        <p>Our mat Pilates classes follow the classical progression with modern modifications:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Centering:</strong> Breath work and pelvic floor activation to start</li>
            <li><strong>Abdominal series:</strong> The hundred, roll-up, single-leg stretch, double-leg stretch, spine stretch</li>
            <li><strong>Side-lying work:</strong> Outer thigh and hip strengthening</li>
            <li><strong>Prone work:</strong> Back extension and spinal articulation</li>
            <li><strong>Seated work:</strong> Spinal rotation and hip flexor length</li>
            <li><strong>Final relaxation:</strong> Integration and release</li>
        </ul>
        
        <p>Classes are 50-60 minutes and suitable for all levels. We offer modifications for beginners and advanced variations for experienced practitioners.</p>
        
        <h2>The Heat Advantage</h2>
        <p>Our 30-32°C infrared heat makes mat Pilates even more effective:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Warmed muscles:</strong> Your body is ready to work from the first minute</li>
            <li><strong>Deeper stretches:</strong> The heat allows your connective tissue to release more fully</li>
            <li><strong>Increased circulation:</strong> Blood flow enhances muscle activation and recovery</li>
            <li><strong>Detoxification:</strong> Deep sweating complements the internal work</li>
            <li><strong>Joint protection:</strong> Warm joints move more safely and fluidly</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Who Is This For?</h2>
        <p>Mat Pilates is for everyone, but it's especially beneficial for:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Core weakness:</strong> Build genuine abdominal strength from the inside out</li>
            <li><strong>Back pain:</strong> Spinal alignment and deep core support relieve pressure</li>
            <li><strong>Posture issues:</strong> Shoulder and hip alignment work corrects sitting habits</li>
            <li><strong>Athletes:</strong> Core stability transfers to every sport</li>
            <li><strong>Pre/post-natal:</strong> Pelvic floor and deep core work (with modifications)</li>
            <li><strong>Tourists:</strong> Perfect recovery after surfing, hiking, or travel</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Pricing</h2>
        <p><strong>Drop-In:</strong> €22 (buy 1, get 1 free for first-timers)<br>
        <strong>Vacation Week:</strong> €59 unlimited<br>
        <strong>Intro Offer:</strong> €79 for 14 days unlimited</p>
        
